## [upstream] min: fix the parabolic-step test in the Brent minimiser

Commit: c27559ec6

`brent_iterate()` takes the parabolic step `p/q` only when the trial point
`u = z + p/q` lies inside the bracket.  With `q` made positive that is
`-q*w_lower < p < q*w_upper`, but the code tested `p < q*w_lower`, which
admits trial points below `x_left` and rejects many valid parabolic steps,
forcing golden-section steps.  A transcription error from Brent's Algol 60;
netlib `fmin`, Numerical Recipes, Forsythe et al. and Boost all have the
corrected form.

Files: `min/brent.c`, plus a regression test in `min/test.c`/`min/test_funcs.c`.

See Savannah bug #43496.


## [upstream] monte: avoid inf weight in VEGAS when the box variance is subnormal

Commit: e3cab2d02

`gsl_monte_vegas_integrate()` computed `wgt = 1/var` whenever `var > 0`.
A tiny but non-zero subnormal `var` makes `1/var` overflow to `+Inf`, which
propagates into `wtd_int_sum` and makes the result (and `chisq`) `NaN`.
Any `var` for which `1/var` is not finite is now treated as zero.

Files: `monte/vegas.c`, plus a regression test in `monte/test.c`.

See Savannah bug #44612.


## [upstream] roots: initialise Newton and Steffenson with the combined fdf call

Commit: 4eac6584f

Both fdfsolvers initialised with separate `GSL_FN_FDF_EVAL_F` and
